        {
          "label": "study_title",
          "text": "Single-cell RNA-seq data of C. elegans early embryos."
        },
        {
          "label": "study_abstract",
          "text": "We performed single-cell transcriptional profiling of Caenorhabditis elegans embryos to benchmark CONCORD, a dimensionality reduction and data integration framework for single-cell analysis. This dataset complements previously published late-stage embryogenesis transcriptomic studies by enriching for early-stage embryos through low-temperature culture conditions, enabling construction of a comprehensive, continuous map of the full embryogenesis process. Overall design: Wildtype N2 worms were grown on NGM plates and synchronized by bleaching. Eggs hatched on 10-cm plates and grown until L3/L4 stage. Then, plates were transferred to a 12\u00c2\u00b0C and incubated for 48 h. Adult worms were lysed by bleaching, and embryos were dissociated into single cells. Cells were loaded onto a Chromium GEM-X chip, libraries were prepared following the 10x Genomics protocol."
        }
      ],
